-- title:
--   Agreement of places for two q-expansion-pinned models of X₀(N₀)
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, and a datum $M : \mathrm{LevelModel}\ N_0\ q\ A$, among whose fields are a curve model $M.\mathrm{Meta}_0$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}(X_0(N_0)) =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N₀` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ and an isomorphism $M.\mathrm{eeta}_0$ from its underlying scheme to the pullback of `igusaTo N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbf Z_{(q)} \to \overline{\mathbf Q}$. Assume the element $\bar j =$ `CharPModel.jBar N₀` (the coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar N₀` of the $q$-expansion of $j$) is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ and nonzero, and that `modularFunctionFieldBar N₀` is finite-dimensional over each of $\overline{\mathbf Q}(\bar j)$ and $\overline{\mathbf Q}(\bar j^{-1})$. Assume given an $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-algebra isomorphism $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ from $\overline{\mathbf Q} \otimes_{\mathbf Z_{(q)}} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ N_0\ q$ (the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull N₀` integral over $\mathbf Z_{(q)}[j]$) onto $\mathrm{chartRing}\ \overline{\mathbf Q}\ \{\bar j\}$ (the elements integral over $\overline{\mathbf Q}[\bar j]$), which on $1 \otimes b$ is given by applying `coeffEmb` to the Laurent series $b$, so that $e_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ is pinned by $q$-expansions. Put $M_\eta := \mathrm{CurveModel.ofGenerator}\ \overline{\mathbf Q}\ \bar j$, the model obtained by gluing the two charts determined by $\bar j$ and $\bar j^{-1}$. The assertion is: for every morphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to the same pullback which is an isomorphism, satisfies $e_\eta$ followed by `pullback.snd` $= M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$, and is chart-compatible in the sense that `CurveModel.ι₀` followed by $e_\eta$ and then `pullback.fst` equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map $e_{\mathrm{Fin}} \circ \mathrm{includeRight}$ followed by `ιFin N₀ q`, and for every $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-point $x$ of $M_\eta.C$ over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ and every $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-point $x_0$ of $M.\mathrm{Meta}_0.C$ over its structure morphism, if $x$ followed by $e_\eta$ equals $x_0$ followed by $M.\mathrm{eeta}_0$, then the two points determine the same place of `modularFunctionFieldBar N₀` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ under the bijections `pointEquivPlace` of $M_\eta$ and of $M.\mathrm{Meta}_0$ respectively.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre comparison step: the geometric generic fibre of the Igusa scheme, presented once through the level datum $M$ and once through the model generated by $\bar j$, induces the same identification of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points with places of the function field of $X_0(N_0)$, both identifications being normalised by reading chart functions as their $q$-expansions. It is used in the Deligne–Rapoport model package to locate sections and closed points at the crossing of the reduction and to compare the two reduction maps.
-- source:
